*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*      MLINK -- linkage segment for the Go SIL machine
*
*      S4D58 6.20: "MLINK is a file of entry points and external symbol
*      names that describe linkages used to access machine-language
*      subroutines and I/O packages."
*
*      This machine has no machine-language subroutines and no external
*      I/O package.  The operations that would need them -- OUTPUT,
*      STPRNT, STREAD, BKSPCE, ENFILE, REWIND, MSTIME, DATE, LOAD, LINK,
*      UNLOAD -- are implemented by the VM against a host interface it
*      owns, so nothing in this segment has to be declared to the
*      assembler.
*
*      MLINK therefore assembles no data and defines no symbols.  It is
*      kept as a segment rather than deleted because COPY MLINK is in
*      the historical source (line 225) and that source is read-only.
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
